WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.000
Case 4: the file gains a new column, discount_code. Everything else is the same. (Re-run recorded after the fact.)

00:07.000 --> 00:15.000
Step 1 done (uploaded). Step 2: run the same pipeline.

00:15.000 --> 00:18.000
"Pipeline completed successfully." This is the one case Rhombus handles well.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.000
The 8 known columns come out exactly as before.

00:22.000 --> 00:25.000
But the table ends at status. discount_code was quietly dropped, and nothing tells you.

00:25.000 --> 00:28.000
Step 3: the new file is in Google Cloud Storage. Fine, unless the business needed that column.
